    },
    "comprehensive_coverage": {
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "rationale": "The pool reaches past plain take-away into comparison subtraction: seed 44 asks how many fewer medals a friend has and seed 602 does the same with knee pads. With regrouping (90 less 26, 73 less 67) and without (42 less 10, 31 less 10) are both represented."
    },
    "cognitive_capacity": {
      "verdict": "CONCERN",
      "rationale": "Seed 600 opens with 'A art room', an article error in text meant to be read to or by a young child. The contexts also strain plausibility, as when a home desk is said to hold 98 canvases in seed 501, which invites a child to doubt the scenario rather than solve it."
    },
    "variant_comprehensiveness": {
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "rationale": "Stair-descending, counting back, comparison, removal from a room, giving away to friends, a pictured set, a true-or-false claim and a peer's solution to check all appear across these seeds. For an orally-or-pictorially delivered competency that is the right spread."
    },
    "competency_alignment": {
      "verdict": "CONCERN",
      "rationale": "Two seeds subtract nothing at all: Des goes down 0 steps in seed 72 and Moses takes away 0 baskets in seed 601, both keyed True. Zero-subtrahend items test reading comprehension, not the with-and-without-regrouping progression this node is supposed to build."
    },
    "scale_appropriateness": {
      "verdict": "CONCERN",
      "rationale": "Seed 42 works with 4 minus 1, well under the two-digit territory implied by numbers less than 100, and several distractor slots break the other way: 116 is offered against 90 less 26 and 113 against 60 less 53, both larger than the starting quantity."
